{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2952","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2952","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2952\",\"parent_revision\":\"1bbfabff35de737dc93b725e3709c8882232fdab\",\"root_revision\":\"3018aa3ed6e9dd06d858d80d1a1a05725eb11999b8ed7f62c8038544fb16b5f7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-17\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n62 SKILL.md files use the `$ARGUMENTS` bang-exec dynamic-context-injection pattern; 23 use bang-exec generally. The `work-backlog-item` skill's own parser (`parse.mjs`) was found and fixed in PR #2951: `$ARGUMENTS` was spliced verbatim into a double-quoted shell string, so free text containing a double quote \u2014 including the skill's own documented invocation example \u2014 broke the outer quoting, and embedded parens/backticks/`#` were then parsed as real shell syntax. The fix routes the text through a quoted-delimiter heredoc piped via stdin instead.\\n\\nIt is not known whether any of the other 61 skills using `$ARGUMENTS` in a bang-exec line have the same fragility, a different fragility, or none at all \u2014 each has its own bang-exec line shape and hasn't been individually checked.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: The accepted fix pattern for `work-backlog-item` was a quoted-delimiter heredoc (`<<'EOF'`) piped via stdin, with `shell: bash` pinned in frontmatter since heredocs are bash-only syntax. Whether that same pattern applies to another skill needs to be verified against that skill's own invocation shape, not assumed.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **skill.md bang-exec lines across the repo splice $arguments into shell-quoted strings without an audited safety pattern** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 found while fixing work-backlog-item's parser in PR #2951\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"da55f49a13e287c2f2f58bd8acc804d13586e7a8793ca971a6bff89db0cfbac4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgwVuA\"}"}